{"entryId":"3139","paragraphs":[{"sourceId":"heilprin:sefaria-warsaw:ta:3139:1","sourceSha256":"1de29a67dbab015ee7e1a9cf60b61c4d6095a6467ad02f59f105061c178a79e3","englishSha256":"566dd46683c6f6b4f395407f5eee12ed0ad3e7e9e5590f1edcb395ba00be567f","citations":[{"id":"3139:1:link-001","he":[21,55],"en":[33,87],"target":{"entry":48,"paragraph":1},"reference":"Seder HaDorot, Tanaim and Amoraim 48:1","assessment":"The earlier heading exists and preserves its own dossier. The pointer does not settle Heilprin’s conjecture.","evidence":[{"reference":"Seder HaDorot 48:1","target":{"entry":48,"paragraph":1},"witness":"Pinned Warsaw digital witness"}]},{"id":"3139:1:link-002","he":[57,81],"en":[88,129],"target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Moed_Katan_28a.16"},"reference":"Moed Katan 28a:16","assessment":"Rava explicitly seeks this Rabbah’s humility. Piety is Heilprin’s characterization; the cited wish names humility.","evidence":[{"reference":"Moed Katan 28a:16","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Moed_Katan_28a.16"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"}]},{"id":"3139:1:link-003","he":[82,122],"en":[135,204],"target":{"entry":3147,"paragraph":1},"reference":"Seder HaDorot, Tanaim and Amoraim 3147:1","assessment":"Bavli records the curse after the trees were cut and limits the outcome to the lifetime of Rabbah bar Rav Huna.","evidence":[{"reference":"Seder HaDorot 3147:1","target":{"entry":3147,"paragraph":1},"witness":"Pinned Warsaw digital witness"},{"reference":"Bava Metzia 108a:3","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Bava_Metzia_108a.3"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"}]},{"id":"3139:1:link-004","he":[124,165],"en":[206,320],"target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Sotah_49a.10"},"reference":"Sotah 49a:10","assessment":"The named digital Bavli reads Abba for the grandson. Heilprin’s parallel entry quotes Rava and brings independent explicit testimony to a son named Rava. Keep the story’s name variant distinct from the genealogical claim.","evidence":[{"reference":"Sotah 49a:10","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Sotah_49a.10"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"},{"reference":"Seder HaDorot 3087:1","target":{"entry":3087,"paragraph":1},"witness":"Pinned Warsaw digital witness"},{"reference":"Chullin 76a:12","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Chullin_76a.12"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"}]},{"id":"3139:1:link-005","he":[167,205],"en":[321,394],"target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Moed_Katan_25a.24"},"reference":"Moed Katan 25a:24","assessment":"Bavli attests that the two were brought up together. Its following passage depicts the two coffins at the bridge.","evidence":[{"reference":"Moed Katan 25a:24","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Moed_Katan_25a.24"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"},{"reference":"Moed Katan 25b:1","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Moed_Katan_25b.1"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"}]},{"id":"3139:1:link-006","he":[212,252],"en":[396,453],"target":{"entry":498,"paragraph":1},"reference":"Seder HaDorot, Tanaim and Amoraim 498:1","assessment":"The pointed-to entry quotes Gelei Eretz Yisrael’s cave tradition. The Bavli corroborates arrival from Babylonia only. The topographic tradition remains attributed.","evidence":[{"reference":"Seder HaDorot 498:1","target":{"entry":498,"paragraph":1},"witness":"Pinned Warsaw digital witness"},{"reference":"Moed Katan 25b:1","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Moed_Katan_25b.1"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"}]},{"id":"3139:1:link-007","he":[254,335],"en":[468,483],"target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Moed_Katan_25a.24"},"reference":"Moed Katan 25a:24","assessment":"The named Bavli reads Rabbah bar Huna and calls the speaker a boy, with the eulogy over the folio boundary. Rav bar Rav Huna reflects Heilprin’s printed wording and is retained.","evidence":[{"reference":"