2047],"target":{"entry":957,"paragraph":1},"reference":"Seder HaDorot, Tanaim and Amoraim 957:1","assessment":"The earlier dossier expressly distinguishes the exilarch from the Babylonian namesake and flags further consideration.","evidence":[{"reference":"Seder HaDorot 957:1","target":{"entry":957,"paragraph":1},"witness":"Pinned Warsaw digital witness"},{"reference":"Rashi on Moed Katan 25b:2:1","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Rashi_on_Moed_Katan_25b.2.1"},"witness":"Vilna Edition"}]},{"id":"3139:1:link-016","he":[1143,1192],"en":[2121,2146],"target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Berakhot_53b.26"},"reference":"Berakhot 53b:26","assessment":"Both passages present Rav first telling his own son Hiyya to seize the blessing, then Rav Huna telling his son Rabbah the same. In the checked versions only Rav’s preceding address explicitly includes “my son.”","evidence":[{"reference":"Berakhot 53b:26","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Berakhot_53b.26"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"},{"reference":"Nazir 66b:1","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Nazir_66b.1"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"}]},{"id":"3139:1:link-017","he":[1143,1192],"en":[2151,2163],"target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Nazir_66b.1"},"reference":"Nazir 66b:1","assessment":"Both passages present Rav first telling his own son Hiyya to seize the blessing, then Rav Huna telling his son Rabbah the same. In the checked versions only Rav’s preceding address explicitly includes “my son.”","evidence":[{"reference":"Nazir 66b:1","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Nazir_66b.1"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"}]},{"id":"3139:1:link-018","he":[1194,1219],"en":[2165,2176],"target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Shevuot_31a.10"},"reference":"Shevuot 31a:10","assessment":"The name is Rava bar Rav Huna at the instruction to litigants.","evidence":[{"reference":"Shevuot 31a:10","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Shevuot_31a.10"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"}]},{"id":"3139:1:link-019","he":[1230,1236],"en":[2209,2220],"target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Shabbat_10a.2"},"reference":"Shabbat 10a:2","assessment":"Rava bar Rav Huna dresses for prayer in this section. The same folio gives Rabbah in the Rav Hisda scene.","evidence":[{"reference":"Shabbat 10a:2","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Shabbat_10a.2"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"}]},{"id":"3139:1:link-020","he":[1238,1244],"en":[2222,2226],"target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Shabbat_66b.5"},"reference":"Shabbat 66b:5","assessment":"The garment interpretation is attributed to Rava bar Rav Huna.","evidence":[{"reference":"Shabbat 66b:5","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Shabbat_66b.5"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"}]},{"id":"3139:1:link-021","he":[1246,1254],"en":[2227,2239],"target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Shabbat_89a.7"},"reference":"Shabbat 89a:7","assessment":"The checked digital text reads Rabbah, son of Rav Huna, paired with Rav Hisda. Heilprin lists it among Rava spellings.","evidence":[{"reference":"Shabbat 89a:7","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Shabbat_89a.7"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"}]},{"id":"3139:1:link-022","he":[1256,1262],"en":[2241,2246],"target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Shabbat_104b.6"},"reference":"Shabbat 104b:6","assessment":"The letter-writing interpretation is attributed to Rava bar Rav Huna.","evidence":[{"reference":"Shabbat 104b:6","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Shabbat_104b.6"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"}]},{"id":"3139:1:link-023","he":[1264,1281],"en":[2247,2272],"target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Bava_Batra_136b.11"},"reference":"Bava Batra 136b:11","assessment":"The checked digital text has Rabbah bar Rav Huna challenging Rav. Heilprin lists the folio among Rava occurrences.","evidence":[{"reference":"Bava Batra 136b:11","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Bava_Batra_136b.11"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"}]},{"id":"3139:1:link-024","he":[1283,1321],"en":[2273,2326],"target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Berakhot_45b.10"},"reference":"Berakhot 45b:10","assessment":"The Bavli reads Rava bar Rav Huna addressing Rav Huna. The asserted paternal reading is the entry’s inference.","evidence":[{"reference":"Berakhot 45b:10","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Berakhot_45b.10"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"}]},{"id":"3139:1:link-025","he":[1323,1379],"en":[2328,2452],"target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Shabbat_121b.6"},"reference":"Shabbat 121b:6","assessment":"The checked text reads Rava. Rabbah is Heilprin’s explicit emendation, not a reading substituted here.","evidence":[{"reference":"Shabbat 121b:6","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Shabbat_121b.6"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"}]},{"id":"3139:1:link-026","he":[1381,1417],"en":[2453,2511],"target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Chullin_76a.12"},"reference":"Chullin 76a:12","assessment":"Explicit genealogy in Hullin, independent of the date story’s Abba/Rava variation.","evidence":[{"reference":"Chullin 76a:12","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Chullin_76a.12"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"}]},{"id":"3139:1:link-027","he":[1419,1479],"en":[2512,2606],"target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Gittin_29b.16"},"reference":"Gittin 29b:16","assessment":"The father-to-Rav chain is explicit.","evidence":[{"reference":"Gittin 29b:16","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Gittin_29b.16"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"}]},{"id":"3139:1:link-028","he":[1481,1557],"en":[2763,2783],"target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Shabbat_81b.6"},"reference":"Shabbat 81b:6","assessment":"The matron, and then the sages, acts upon the boat, which the verb explicitly names.","evidence":[{"reference":"Shabbat 81b:6","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Shabbat_81b.6"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"}]},{"id":"3139:1:link-029","he":[1559,1586],"en":[2785,2832],"target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Gittin_76b.8"},"reference":"Gittin 76b:8","assessment":"The formula recurs in Gittin. Abba bar Zavda sends the legal inquiry through Mari bar Mar; the catalogue does not identify him with “my father and master.”","evidence":[{"reference":"Gittin 76b:8","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Gittin_76b.8"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"},{"reference":"Gittin 86b:25","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Gittin_86b.25"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"},{"reference":"Gittin 86b:26","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Gittin_86b.26"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"}]},{"id":"3139:1:link-030","he":[1588,1609],"en":[2833,2862],"target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Chullin_124b.13"},"reference":"Chullin 124b:13","assessment":"Exact question from Rav Avya to Rabbah bar Rav Huna.","evidence":[{"reference":"Chullin 124b:13","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Chullin_124b.13"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"}]},{"id":"3139:1:link-031","he":[1624,1649],"en":[2938,2948],"target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Chullin_76a.12"},"reference":"Chullin 76a:12","assessment":"Rabbah bar Rav Huna is the reporting subject. He reports Rav Ashi; his son Rava reports Rav Asi in the same sentence.","evidence":[{"reference":"Chullin 76a:12","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Chullin_76a.12"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"}]},{"id":"3139:1:link-032","he":[1651,1660],"en":[2950,3027],"target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Kiddushin_42a.7"},"reference":"Kiddushin 42a:7","assessment":"The Bavli’s matching chain is Rava bar Rav Huna → Rav Giddel → Rav. Preserve the variant spelling 